WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.746
The plan sets the hill, but the legs are yours. Telo Ride now lets the rider take

00:00:07.746 --> 00:00:09.321
over the resistance.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.564
Raise resistance moves the target up one level and sends it. Lower resistance moves

00:00:15.564 --> 00:00:16.622
it down one.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.621
At thirty-two it stays thirty-two, and at one it stays one. Every change is clamped

00:00:25.621 --> 00:00:26.940
before it's sent.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.691
Before any target, a nudge starts from the resistance the bike reports. Eight

00:00:35.691 --> 00:00:36.788
becomes nine.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.246
Picking a level sets it outright. Level twenty is sent as twenty, marked as the

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.298
rider's own.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.553
A change by hand lasts until the segment ends. When the next one starts, the plan's

00:00:56.553 --> 00:00:58.042
level applies again.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.726
With the bike away, or refusing control, nothing is sent by hand, and the target

00:01:06.726 --> 00:01:08.162
stays where it was.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.460
Each command remembers where it came from, the plan or the rider, with its

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.950
acknowledgement time.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.443
Still to come: the steppers and level bars on the ride screens, switched off with no

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:28.032
bike.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.664
Home doesn't change yet, at any width. The rider's changes wait in the engine for

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.961
the ride screens.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.756
What the tests prove: seven new unit tests, one per row of the requirement, and

00:01:47.756 --> 00:01:49.372
every spec still green.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:58.164
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.021
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.692
every hill and interval.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:10.215
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:02:10.215 --> 00:02:15.663
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:18.653
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:21.491
A custom workout lives under Profile.
